    "turns": 37,
    "tool_calls": 37,
    "summary": "Fixed the wfmt package to satisfy the specification. Key changes:\n\n1. **varint.py**: Fixed `decode_uvarint` to properly handle multi-byte LEB128 encoding (was only reading 1 byte and masking with 0x7F). Now correctly accumulates 7-bit groups with continuation bit handling.\n\n2. **crc.py**: Replaced custom CRC implementation with `binascii.crc32` for standard IEEE CRC-32. Fixed `unpack_crc` to raise `WFormatError(\"truncated\")` instead of `ValueError`.\n\n3. **header.py**: Changed count field from big-endian (`>I`) to little-endian (`<I`) to match the actual sample format.\n\n4. **codec.py**: \n   - Added 4-byte alignment padding between records (relative to record area start). This was the critical missing piece - records are padded with zero bytes to ALIGN boundaries.\n   - Updated `pack()` to insert alignment padding after each record.\n   - Updated `unpack()` to skip alignment padding and verify CRC.\n   - All structural errors now raise `WFormatError` with appropriate `kind`.\n   - `verify()`",
    "changed_workspace": true
  },
